id: pm-rust-wdj4
title: Reduce native list and get latency on large indexed trackers
description: "The final parser-cleanup release receipt on a complete 2991-item public tracker copy measured 30 cold processes per command/runtime: native list p50 2116.0 ms versus oracle 1269.9 ms, and native get p50 1864.8 ms versus oracle 1118.5 ms. This is a shared 4-CPU host with effective nice 15, warm filesystem and oracle derived caches; sampled 1-minute load ranged 13.84 to 25.64. Earlier completed receipts also showed slower native list/get. Investigate selective lookup or validated derived indexes without weakening authoritative read correctness, concurrency or parity. Keep this optimization separate from the orientation command slice."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,performance,rust
created_at: "2026-10-18T06:28:16.861Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T20:00:08.961Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Measure the same 30-run commands and retain byte parity, storage integrity and all coverage dimensions."
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:05:58.773Z",codex-agent,"Prerequisite PR #92 is merged into main. Implemented directory-derived strict get lookup, streamed list and brief-context projections, metadata-first filtered search and bounded first-page hit retention. No persistent index is added; release approval remains unset. Plan: byte differential suites unchanged, generated 3000-item latency and portable item-open gates on Linux/macOS/Windows, copied-public-tracker 30-run measurements, exact release checks and an open PR under pm-rust-u4al."
  "2026-10-18T18:06:03.318Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: reverted only Workspace::get to its original read_items-based lookup, rebuilt and ran cargo test --locked --lib workspace::tests::single_item_get. Exit 101, 0 passed, 2 failed: unrelated merge-marker damage broke the target read and duplicate filenames yielded the wrong refusal. Restored lookup: 2 passed, 0 failed. The real 3000-item regression observes exactly one authoritative file open for success and zero for missing or duplicate IDs. The unchanged committed history prefix is retained byte-for-byte. An unpublished local draft whose linked-test stderr captured compiler paths was quarantined unchanged; public task events were replayed from that prefix and linked tests now use a path-redacting wrapper."
  "2026-10-18T18:09:17.030Z",codex-agent,"Pre-PR evidence: 247 library tests passed, both restored lookup tests passed through the sanitized linked-test runner, fmt/pedantic clippy/private-item rustdoc/changelog checks passed, and cargo audit passed with the repository-allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 warning. Real public-copy strace: get item opens 2991 -> 1; total openat 3009 -> 19; history opens zero in both. Paired 30-run runtime measurements and the unchanged affected differential suites are in progress. Generated local latency samples exceeded the unchanged ceilings under shared-host contention; dedicated three-OS CI is the acceptance gate."
  "2026-10-18T18:11:08.269Z",codex-agent,"Opened PR #94. New latency jobs also follow the existing repository workflow contracts: full Git history and tags, locked oracle installation and explicit oracle root. First 30-run paired get result in milliseconds: before p50/p95 1779.3/3062.6, native 12.5/42.3, oracle 1274.5/3346.3. Remaining command samples are running. No source changes after the measured native release build; current follow-up changes only the CI setup."
  "2026-10-18T18:17:01.176Z",codex-agent,"CI timing results on the first implementation: Linux get/list/context p95 5.3/55.8/95.1 ms; macOS 8.3/123.6/113.2 ms; Windows 13.9/179.7/205.9 ms. Windows list failed the required 150 ms ceiling. Removed per-item metadata calls from streamed queries by reusing directory-entry types, narrowed brief-context decoding to its exact ranking/agenda fields, and made SDK summary lists stream instead of materializing full documents. Retaining all thresholds and the unchanged differential suites. A fresh clone with isolated home passed strict tracker health; the non-isolated host showed a global extension version skew, unrelated to tracker integrity."
  "2026-10-18T18:38:32.213Z",codex-agent,"Second Windows timing receipt: get/list/context p95 21.0/204.5/278.7 ms on a slower runner. Removed unneeded dependency/parent index construction and relationship decoding from ordinary list/search metadata filters; unknown-tag discovery now runs only for tag filters. First-page producer limits truncate documents before JSON projection while preserving the full total and cursors. Brief context caches deadline/update/history-recency sort keys and parses its invariant read clock once. New timestamp-count regression passes; 248 library tests and pedantic clippy pass locally. All three OS normal test jobs passed at the preceding source candidate (Linux 473, macOS 469, Windows 464 tests). Thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T19:08:50.894Z",codex-agent,"The CPU-only candidate still missed Windows list/context p95 (189.1/275.0 ms). Added Windows-only bounded filesystem prefetch: four scoped workers, at most 256 raw documents per batch, ordered decoding on the caller; direct get bypasses it. No persistent cache or threshold change. Linux and Windows-GNU pedantic clippy pass. Added real blocked-directory and invalid-UTF-8 storage-refusal cases across public reads, selected-payload strict search checks, duplicate-filename stream sorting and SDK summary sorting/filter tests. These address the macOS aggregate missing error-path regions and comparator coverage without exclusions or threshold reductions. Local storage acceptance: 250 library tests and 13 read-contract tests passed."
  "2026-10-18T19:27:36.130Z",codex-agent,"Final source receipt 1095e6a: generated-fixture CI latency passed on Linux/macOS/Windows with unchanged 50/150/250 ms ceilings. P95 get/list/context ms: Linux 4.1/45.0/85.0; macOS 15.6/101.4/168.8; Windows 15.8/86.0/141.9. Both portable get regressions passed on every OS. Final real-copy comparison completed 30 native and 30 pinned-oracle cold processes per command; baseline has 30 samples per command. All 6005 captured authoritative hashes remain identical in the 2991-item copy. The live source advanced independently; it was only copied and hashed, never passed to either CLI. Source and binary fingerprints, 360 raw samples, p50/p95 tables and per-OS samples are linked in docs."
  "2026-10-18T19:27:38.862Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioural revert proof: reverted only the context ordering/scoring changes to their pre-cache versions; cargo test --locked --lib list::tests::context_timestamp_parse_work_is_linear exited 101 with 0 passed and 1 failed (346 timestamp parses against a 282 bound). Restored implementation: 1 passed. The three linked commands also passed: lookup 2 tests, context parse-work 1, selected search-payload strictness 1. Project test-result tracking is disabled, so these results are recorded here without changing that policy. Public receipt output is path-redacted, including temporary and escaped Windows paths. Aggregate CI conformance and all four 100 percent coverage dimensions remain required before handoff."
  "2026-10-18T19:40:40.273Z",codex-agent,"CI at 1095e6a passed all three ordinary Rust jobs and all three generated-fixture latency jobs. All nine p95 ceilings passed unchanged; portable lookup regressions passed twice per OS. The release aggregates pass behavior but refuse coverage at 100% lines/functions, 99.95% regions and 99.93% branches. Adding real filesystem refusal and SDK selection integration/unit cases for both compiled library variants; production source and measured binary remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T19:44:03.499Z",codex-agent,"Final local validation: cargo fmt --all -- --check passed; cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings passed, including the Windows GNU cross-target run; cargo test --locked --lib workspace::tests passed 13 tests; cargo test --locked --test read_contract passed 16 tests. Instrumented lib plus read-contract run passed 252 and 16 tests and exercised the initializer/error paths missing from the previous full CI coverage report. Four linked commands passed (2, 1, 1 and 13 tests); project test-result tracking is disabled, so the CLI returned recorded=false and results are documented here without changing policy. Final full three-OS aggregates must still certify all four coverage dimensions at unchanged 100% thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T19:44:13.235Z",codex-agent,"Publishing benchmark documentation and raw receipts with the final test-only coverage repair. Runtime source remains exactly 1095e6a. Releasing ownership for CI and orchestrator review; leave the item in progress and the PR open. No merge, tag, release approval or publishing enablement is authorized. Final exact-head CI results and the comparison tables are maintained in PR #94."
  "2026-10-18T19:47:22.657Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI exposed a test expectation bug on macOS: temporary paths use a logical spelling while Workspace canonicalizes the tracker, so an exact error-path assertion compared different aliases. Canonicalize the expected locked directory before applying the real refusal. Production source, coverage thresholds and latency fixture remain unchanged. Reclaiming only to repair the cross-platform test expectation."
  "2026-10-18T19:48:15.741Z",codex-agent,"The canonical expected-path correction passed cargo test --locked --lib workspace::tests::streamed_queries_refuse_unlistable_nested_directory (1 passed), cargo fmt --all -- --check, and cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings. Release ownership again with the test-only fix; exact-head three-OS CI remains required and will be reported in PR #94. Production measurements and revert proofs are unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T19:54:54.172Z",codex-agent,"The corrected-head macOS timing gate passed get/context but failed list at 192.96 ms p95 against the unchanged 150 ms ceiling. Linux passed all ceilings; Windows also passed all ceilings. Extend the existing bounded four-worker raw-file prefetch to macOS, preserving serial decoding, file order and refusal order. Direct get remains outside prefetch. No timing threshold, fixture or oracle contract changes; rerun exact-head CI and verify Linux benchmark binary identity or refresh its samples."
  "2026-10-18T20:00:05.235Z",codex-agent,"macOS now uses the existing Windows bounded prefetch implementation: four workers, at most 256 raw files, serial ordered decoding and no prefetch for get. Linux remains serial. cargo fmt --all -- --check, pedantic clippy and release build passed. The rebuilt Linux executable is byte-identical to the measured binary: SHA-256 4f9ac7345f1303cc9967ce0856efdbce0665553956e7dad81a2596c650e54ed5, so the 360 public-tracker samples and open counts apply unchanged. Final exact-head macOS latency and all three release aggregates remain required; thresholds and fixture are unchanged. Releasing ownership for CI and review again."
